abstract: >-
  Frozen software snapshot for the JMIR AI manuscript "Predicting 30-Day
  Hospital Readmission in Medicare Patients: An Interpretable
  Gradient-Boosting Model on MIMIC-IV v3.1". Contains the leakage-safe,
  development-only staged recursive feature elimination pipeline and the
  final consensus-31 XGBoost model (src/pipeline_v5_v6), canonical
  machine-readable results (results_v6/final_model_v6.json and companions),
  publication figures, the reproducibility report, the value-level
  consistency report, and the 207-predictor audit workbook. Three evidence
  tiers: development-data out-of-fold AUROC of the complete selection
  procedure 0.7748 (95% CI 0.7715 to 0.7782, primary), grouped development
  cross-validation of the fixed consensus-31 set 0.7756 (secondary), and
  0.7738 (95% CI 0.7671 to 0.7804) on the historically exposed test
  partition (tertiary). Same-cohort baselines: adapted LACE 0.605 and
  12-month HOSPITAL 0.649. MIMIC-IV row-level data are not included, per
  the PhysioNet Credentialed Health Data Use Agreement.
keywords:
